# Clean Architecture

## Dependency rule (never violate)
```
presentation ──► domain ◄── data
```
- `domain/` is pure Dart: **no** imports of Flutter, `dio`, `shared_preferences`, JSON, or `data/`.
- `presentation/` imports `domain/` only (entities, use cases). Never import `data/` models or data sources.
- `data/` implements `domain/` contracts. Only `injection_container.dart` wires concrete classes.

## Feature structure
```
lib/feature/<feature>/
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/        # immutable, Equatable, no fromJson
│   ├── repositories/    # abstract contracts returning Future<Either<Failure, T>>
│   └── usecases/        # one public call() per class, single responsibility
├── data/
│   ├── model/           # fromJson/toJson + toEntity(); defensive parsing
│   ├── datasource/      # <x>_remote_data_source.dart (Dio) + <x>_local_data_source.dart (cache)
│   └── repositories/    # <x>_repository_impl.dart: orchestrates remote/local, maps exceptions → Failure
└── presentation/
    ├── cubit/           # <x>_cubit.dart + <x>_state.dart
    ├── pages/           # <x>_screen.dart
    └── widget/          # feature-only widgets
```
Shared code lives in `lib/core/` (`constant/`, `network/`, `error/`, `utils/`, `widget/`, `function/`, `app_theme.dart`).

## Use case shape
```dart
abstract class UseCase<T, Params> {
  Future<Either<Failure, T>> call(Params params);
}
class NoParams extends Equatable { @override List<Object?> get props => []; }
```
Use cases stay thin (delegate + pure domain logic such as local filtering). No Dio/JSON here.

## Errors
- Data sources **throw** typed exceptions (`ServerException`, `NetworkException`, `RequestTimeoutException`, `ParsingException`, `CacheException`, `RequestCancelledException`, `UnknownException`); `failureFromException` maps them to `Failure`.
- Repositories **catch** them and **return** `Left(Failure)`. Nothing above data throws.
- Presentation maps `Failure` → localized message key (never show raw exception text).

## DI order in `injection_container.dart`
1. External (`Dio`, `SharedPreferences`, `Connectivity`) → 2. Core (`NetworkInfo`, `DioClient`) → 3. Data sources → 4. Repositories → 5. Use cases → 6. Cubits.
`registerLazySingleton` for 1–5, `registerFactory` for Cubits. App-wide cubits (favorites) are also factories, created once by a `BlocProvider` above the router, which owns and closes them.
